  "question": {
    "text": "The escape velocity of a body on a planet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>km</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The escape velocity of the body on another planet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, whose density is four times and radius is half of the planet <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>, is&nbsp;"
